Cell["\<\
Automatic uses random candidate permutations for bounded sampling and \
deterministic order for All. Identity is deterministic. RandomSample randomly \
permutes candidates with backtracking. RandomChoice retains one random \
candidate at each step without backtracking and is unsupported with All.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9e2ae151-d415-4a9e-bc81-c6168c3a063e"],

Cell["\<\
A callback receives a list of literal total-vertex candidates. It may return \
one member or a duplicate-free list of retained members. A returned list that \
is itself a candidate is read as that one vertex first. A pruning callback \
restricts the search tree: shortage then concerns that retained tree. \
RandomChoice retains at most one complete route, so an exact count above one \
returns {}. Unsupported option names, nominal selectors and callback results \
remain unevaluated. The first duplicate option takes precedence.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"72899689-a639-4e35-b0ae-5cd2191dcf0e"]
}, Open  ]],

